Hmm, but generate returns a promise; fine. Actually simpler: make `go` a plain method record:

```js
go: {
    $method: {
        func: (self) => {
            const closest = self.closest;
            if (closest.distance !== null) {
                self.state.prompt = closest.text;
                return self.generate();
            }
        },
        args: "{self}"
    }
},
generate: {
    $method: {
        func: "fluid.demos.imageGenerator.generate",
        args: ["{self}.state"]
    }
},
showAnother: {...},
refresh: {...}
```

But careful about naming members: our umbrella layer merges over `fluid.demos.imageGenerator`? No — we do NOT include imageGenerator in our $layers. We only subclass closestNoteFinder. So no conflicts with imageGenerator members.

