Template syntax doesn't have @if. Conditional subcomponents via $if. Simplify: show the button always; below it, an error message subcomponent ($if error), a loading message ($if isGenerating), and result figure subcomponent ($if image). These mirror imageGenerator's small subcomponents. Or compute an img tag with src attribute: `src="@{{self}.image.url}"` — but if image is null/unavailable, src binding removes attribute. Then credit line below. Honestly, using $component subcomponents like imageGenerator does is the established pattern in these layers, and keeps styling consistent.

Let me draft the layer:

